{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790995775,"nonce":"DXG8+VUdr3RDiORyYVsPloynZas=","title":"Input lags and empty-space hover burns CPU: hlwindow's poll() costs about 2.6 ms per event","message":"Measured with ASHUI_FRAME_LOG on the interactions demo (tools/demo), macOS, trackpad:\n- 21,658 events took 56.6 s inside window.poll(): about 2.6 ms per call. One frame's batch of 751 events took 1,317 ms to drain, so the UI froze for that long; scroll deltas reached the screen 238 ms late at the median and up to 979 ms.\n- Device events (raw motion; ashui never uses them) are almost half of all events.\n- ashui's own work per frame: flush about 0.1 ms, layout about 6 ms when text changed, display list about 4.4 ms, GPU about 1.6 ms, present about 0.4 ms. An empty-space pointer move costs 0.15 ms and causes no redraw, yet hovering empty space uses 50-90% of a core: it is all in poll().\n\nashui now collapses each batch to its last pointer position and summed wheel delta, so the handlers run once per frame, but the batch still drains slowly. Handed to xwindow-f0 on 2026-10-03: cheap poll (likely one run-loop pump per batch, not per call), device events off, a batch call. Blinc's runner idles at about 0% CPU with ControlFlow::Wait and unhandled device events (blinc_platform_desktop event_loop.rs:274-300).\n\nIf needed before that lands: limit how long a frame drains events, so the UI keeps drawing during a flood.","files":null}]}